### Introduction

My name is Blessing Benard Onuoha and I just started learning Data Analytics. 

Before, I thought Data Analytics was only for geniuses. Now I understand it is simple: We take plenty data, we clean it, and we find story inside it.**

This blog is my learning diary. I will be writing everything I learn here.

### What are Data Analytics Projects?

A Data Analytics project is like a school assignment, but for real life.

Example: A shop in Sohar wants to know why sales are down. My job is to take their sales data, check it, and tell them the reason. That is a project.

I am building my own projects and saving them on GitHub so employers can see my work.

### Analytics in Real Time

I learned that analytics is not only for yesterday's data. Some companies use it LIVE.

Like: When you are using Talabat or Bank Muscat app — they see your data in real time to stop fraud. That is called **Real Time Analytics**. It is happening now-now, not tomorrow.

### Data Analytics in Action

Theory is good, but action is better. 

Data Analytics in action means using it to solve real problems:
- Hospital uses data to know how many beds they need
- Shop uses data to know which product to bring more
- My school can use data to know which subject students fail most

This is why I love this course — it is not just book, it is real life.

### The Project Portfolio (Why I Created GitHub)

My teacher said: "If your work is not on GitHub, you didn't do it."

So I created my portfolio here on GitHub. This is like my CV but better — instead of just saying "I know Excel", I will SHOW my Excel project.

Every project I do — Excel, Tableau, Python — I will upload it here.

### The Importance of Data Analytics

Why is Data Analytics important today?

1. Every company now has data, but few people know how to read it.
2. It helps companies save money and make more profit.
3. For me, it is a skill that can give me a good job in Oman, Dubai, or remote.

In short: Data is the new oil, and Data Analyst is the person who refines it.

### Sharing Your Accomplishments

I learned something big today: **Don't learn in secret.**

When I finish small thing — like creating my GitHub or cleaning one Excel sheet — I should share it. 

Sharing helps me:
- Remember what I learned
- Get feedback from others
- Build confidence

That is why I am writing this blog.

### Introduction to Blogging

Blogging is how I share my accomplishments.

Before today, I thought blogging is only for writers. Now I know Data Analysts also blog to explain what they found.

My plan:
- Every week, I will write one blog about what I learned
- I will keep my English simple so anyone can understand
- I will add charts from Tableau when I learn it

